WEBVTT

00:04.040 --> 00:05.920
<i>The way my heart beat then...</i>

00:07.460 --> 00:09.420
<i>The view I had during that moment...</i>

00:12.300 --> 00:14.430
<i>The smoldering embers in my heart</i>

00:15.470 --> 00:18.180
<i>had become one with the crimson machine...</i>

01:49.350 --> 01:51.810
The bureau has made the decision to enact

01:51.900 --> 01:54.280
the Anti-Subversive
Activities Act in response to the BMA,

01:54.360 --> 01:57.650
the unlawful organization
conducting terrorist acts against the GGP.

01:57.740 --> 02:02.370
The more trouble the terrorists
cause, the more the GGP gets its way.

02:02.450 --> 02:04.660
...warrants for their arrest.

02:04.750 --> 02:07.120
The Anti-Subversive Activities Act--

02:07.790 --> 02:11.670
I guess the GGP's about to get really serious, too...

02:11.750 --> 02:15.460
Yes. The Cabinet and our
agency will probably be forced

02:15.550 --> 02:20.050
to adopt the white RideBacks to maintain public order.

02:20.140 --> 02:22.220
You're certainly faint of heart.

02:22.300 --> 02:25.390
Your own sister is out there
riding those very RideBacks,

02:25.470 --> 02:28.850
without any regard for her family's objections.

02:28.940 --> 02:31.900
Where did she get her bullishness from?

02:34.610 --> 02:35.980
Sorry to bother you.

02:36.690 --> 02:38.070
I should go.

02:38.150 --> 02:40.760
Ryunosuke. Look after Tamayo.

02:43.410 --> 02:45.580
My very soul was shaking!

02:45.660 --> 02:50.330
The brilliant Rin Ogata is
perfect at everything she tries!

02:50.420 --> 02:54.710
Your sense of balance and stuff
is on a different level than other people!

02:54.800 --> 02:58.590
So I think that difference
must be on the genetic level!

02:58.970 --> 03:04.350
You suddenly went soaring
through the air, almost like a Pegasus!

03:04.430 --> 03:07.220
The sight of it struck me right in the heart!

03:07.310 --> 03:09.180
She really went that high up?

03:09.270 --> 03:13.350
Yes! It was a miraculous jump
that practically defied the laws of physics!

03:13.440 --> 03:18.280
You're exaggerating. It was just a jump.
I didn't even think when I did it.

03:18.360 --> 03:20.280
Oh, you're too modest!

03:20.360 --> 03:23.410
That was a beautiful leap only you could have made!

03:23.490 --> 03:25.740
Oh! I wish I could try that too!

03:25.830 --> 03:27.540
Hey! The mayonnaise!

03:29.500 --> 03:32.870
So, who was this prince on
a white horse who came to your rescue?

03:33.080 --> 03:35.040
Apparently he's the club advisor...

03:35.130 --> 03:39.340
Oh! He seemed like a real loner!

03:39.420 --> 03:42.010
And like he could kill a bear with his bare hands...

03:42.090 --> 03:44.340
What kind of prince is that?

03:44.430 --> 03:46.300
What are you doing, Rin?

03:47.010 --> 03:48.810
Hi again!

03:49.020 --> 03:50.930
Oh! She's cute!

03:51.020 --> 03:53.440
Hey, are you the one who wants to join our club?

03:53.520 --> 03:55.400
Oh?! Me?!

03:55.480 --> 03:58.190
--No, it's the girl behind her!
--Huh?

03:58.280 --> 04:00.110
You're Rin Ogata, right?

04:00.190 --> 04:02.280
Sorry about all that trouble yesterday.

04:03.860 --> 04:07.070
I'm Hishida. I'm in my second
year of mechanical engineering.

04:07.160 --> 04:09.120
This is Kawai, he's in his third year.

04:09.410 --> 04:10.450
Nice to meetcha!

04:10.540 --> 04:14.250
So, anyway, we brought the sign-up sheet.

04:14.330 --> 04:17.840
Come visit again sometime!
You can just watch if you want to!

04:17.920 --> 04:20.380
There's usually always someone there!

04:20.710 --> 04:24.510
Hold on, you two! Isn't there
something else you should say first?!

04:24.590 --> 04:25.970
Huh? Like what?

04:26.600 --> 04:30.640
You want Rin to join, after sticking her
in an unsafe, out-of-control vehicle?!

04:30.720 --> 04:32.600
Oh, well, actually...

04:32.680 --> 04:36.600
Yeah! She only made it out
unhurt because of who she is!

04:37.230 --> 04:38.690
I'm really sorry!

04:39.440 --> 04:40.570
See you later!

04:40.650 --> 04:41.820
See you!

04:41.900 --> 04:43.110
Bye!

04:43.610 --> 04:45.360
Looks like she's become attached to you.

04:45.450 --> 04:46.610
Huh?

04:47.660 --> 04:49.030
Sheesh...

04:58.880 --> 05:02.210
Early this morning the GGP's
base in Sasebo was attacked

05:02.300 --> 05:05.130
by the terrorist group known as the BMA.

05:05.220 --> 05:10.350
According to eyewitnesses,
the terrorists used weapons called RideBacks--

05:10.430 --> 05:11.470
Hello?

05:11.560 --> 05:16.020
Are you curious about that
troublemaker girl from yesterday?

05:17.150 --> 05:18.310
What do you mean?

05:18.650 --> 05:23.610
A novice, in the Fuego, making
a jump like that can't just be dumb luck.

05:23.690 --> 05:26.610
Surely you want to know more.

05:27.860 --> 05:29.160
That's her info.

05:29.660 --> 05:35.370
Rin Ogata. Daughter of Yuki Ogata,
the late world-renowned dancer.

05:35.460 --> 05:38.670
She's a ballet thoroughbred;
she's studied it since the age of three

05:38.750 --> 05:42.040
and won top honors at countless competitions.

05:42.670 --> 05:45.050
But given how unsophisticated you are,

05:45.130 --> 05:48.430
I bet you've never even heard of Yuki Ogata.

05:49.930 --> 05:52.160
Drink and you die!!

05:49.930 --> 05:52.160
-Tamayo

06:00.980 --> 06:03.150
It's different from yesterday's...

06:06.240 --> 06:10.200
--"RBZ..."
--That's my machine.

06:10.280 --> 06:12.660
The Fuego's being repaired.

06:12.740 --> 06:14.870
I knew you would come.

06:14.950 --> 06:15.830
Huh? Uhh...

06:15.910 --> 06:18.750
You want to ride a RideBack, don't you?

06:18.830 --> 06:21.540
Oh, no, I just...

06:21.630 --> 06:22.750
You're going to run away?

06:22.840 --> 06:23.880
Run away...?

06:25.170 --> 06:27.550
I can let you ride one.

06:30.760 --> 06:33.890
Face me in a RideBack race!

06:33.970 --> 06:35.850
I'll give you a handicap.

06:35.930 --> 06:41.350
If you can beat me, you're free to
use a RideBack whenever you want!

06:41.440 --> 06:45.400
But, if you lose, you become my servant!

06:46.190 --> 06:48.490
RBZ! Sit!

06:49.110 --> 06:52.070
All right, gifted ballet girl?

06:52.700 --> 06:54.870
I'll get the Fuego ready for you.

06:54.950 --> 06:59.210
The race will be here next Saturday, at 10:00 am.

06:59.290 --> 07:01.170
If you're a no-show, you lose.

07:01.250 --> 07:03.380
W-Wait, hold on...!

07:12.340 --> 07:14.680
S-Servant?!

07:14.760 --> 07:16.760
Are you kidding me? What era is she living in?

07:16.850 --> 07:18.770
She said she'd give me a handicap, though.

07:18.850 --> 07:20.640
That isn't the issue here...

07:20.730 --> 07:23.690
I heard she's president of the RideBack club.

07:24.690 --> 07:27.690
Tamayo Kataoka. Third year French
student and literature club member.

07:27.780 --> 07:29.150
Currently single.

07:29.240 --> 07:32.450
Just where do you get info like that?

07:32.530 --> 07:36.830
So, why would the club president
challenge an amateur like you to a race?

07:36.910 --> 07:38.040
I don't know...

07:38.120 --> 07:41.080
I bet it's because she witnessed that jump too!

07:41.160 --> 07:43.540
That'd make the club president jealous for sure!

07:43.630 --> 07:47.170
I'll definitely be there
to cheer you on! Do your best!

07:47.250 --> 07:49.300
Oh, but I haven't accepted the challenge yet--

07:49.380 --> 07:51.300
Oh, you haven't?

07:51.380 --> 07:54.260
--It's just, you know...
--Oh?

07:54.340 --> 07:58.810
Don't worry about it! I just know you can win!

08:07.440 --> 08:11.190
Yeah. Yeah. You don't have to tell me that.

08:11.280 --> 08:13.450
You're going to school every day, I hope?!

08:13.530 --> 08:15.320
I'm doing club stuff right now.

08:15.410 --> 08:17.870
Urgh. You're full of it again.

08:17.950 --> 08:19.740
Get off my back. I'm hanging up.

08:19.830 --> 08:23.750
Oh, wait, Kenji!
You know a lot about RideBacks, right?

08:23.830 --> 08:27.920
Huh? RideBacks? Sure, no sweat! Ask away!

08:28.000 --> 08:31.210
But why do you wanna know about RideBacks?

08:31.300 --> 08:35.340
Oh, uhh, a friend wants to know more about them, so...

08:35.430 --> 08:36.760
Oh?

08:36.850 --> 08:39.760
Oh, yeah! Doesn't Tamayo Kataoka go to your college?

08:39.850 --> 08:43.100
She won last year's All-Japan RideBack tournament!

08:43.190 --> 08:44.270
Huh?

08:44.350 --> 08:47.230
Do you think you could get her autograph for me?!

08:47.310 --> 08:49.690
I'll tell you whatever you want if you do!

08:54.240 --> 08:56.610
Let's see here...

08:56.700 --> 08:59.660
"Spread Legs Form..."

08:59.740 --> 09:06.000
"To switch to high-speed mode,
lightly pull the second lever

09:06.080 --> 09:11.630
and, under default settings,
press the right foot pedal with your heel."

09:13.260 --> 09:16.130
Was the laundry room open? Hey, Rin!

09:18.300 --> 09:20.680
--What are you doing?
--Nothing.

09:23.020 --> 09:26.690
--Hey, Rin. On Saturday...
--I'm not going to that silly race!

09:26.770 --> 09:30.480
I need to figure out my class schedule and everything,

09:30.570 --> 09:33.530
plus I have so much to do this weekend...

09:34.610 --> 09:36.990
She's totally gonna go.

09:53.380 --> 09:56.590
Why did I feel so excited...?

10:05.930 --> 10:08.310
Think she'll show?

10:10.190 --> 10:12.560
Rin will be here! I know it!

10:15.070 --> 10:18.360
Suzuri, was it? You're really fired up!

10:18.450 --> 10:22.530
Well, I am head of the
"Watch Over Rin Ogata Association!"

10:22.620 --> 10:25.660
RideBacks are fun to ride, you know.

10:26.330 --> 10:28.910
You should try riding one after the race!

10:29.000 --> 10:31.210
Hishida! How are things there?

10:31.290 --> 10:33.090
Still waiting on her.

10:33.170 --> 10:35.130
Is she even gonna come?

10:36.050 --> 10:37.420
Now to set it.

10:40.640 --> 10:42.800
#5 checks out okay.

10:42.890 --> 10:45.720
Okay, now moving on to #6 and #7.

10:45.810 --> 10:46.770
Roger that.

11:04.910 --> 11:07.950
Rin! Hurry! Over here!

11:09.330 --> 11:12.370
Hishida! Lend her my rider suit!

11:12.460 --> 11:14.250
Coming right up!

11:27.930 --> 11:30.140
We thoroughly checked everything this time,

11:30.230 --> 11:31.690
but if anything should happen,

11:31.770 --> 11:35.060
press the emergency
shutdown button on your EW Band.

11:35.150 --> 11:36.270
Okay.

11:36.360 --> 11:37.980
The rules are simple.

11:38.070 --> 11:41.200
We'll take the university's vehicular roads

11:41.280 --> 11:44.910
all the way to the water tower
on the summit and back.

11:44.990 --> 11:46.450
You have a one-lap handicap.

11:46.530 --> 11:50.910
If I don't complete four laps
before you complete three, I lose.

11:51.460 --> 11:54.710
We'll do two laps first so you
can learn the course. Follow me.

11:54.790 --> 11:57.000
That is all. Is that satisfactory?

11:57.090 --> 11:58.130
Yes.

11:58.210 --> 11:59.380
Okay, let's go!

12:02.300 --> 12:05.090
The race will start your third
time around, so don't feel rushed.

12:05.180 --> 12:07.350
Do your best, Rin!

12:07.850 --> 12:09.010
R-Right!

12:13.650 --> 12:16.110
You can do it, Rin!

12:16.480 --> 12:20.980
It was aggressive of Tamayo
to suddenly issue a challenge like that,

12:21.070 --> 12:25.110
but it was especially gutsy
of Rin to accept that challenge.

12:37.250 --> 12:39.250
You're really bookin' it!

12:39.340 --> 12:42.300
I thought you were going
to take it easy at first, Tamayo?

12:42.380 --> 12:45.840
I am. I'm keeping up
with her pace behind me.

12:49.970 --> 12:52.220
She's already here?! Man, she's fast!

13:00.360 --> 13:02.070
Whoa! No way!

13:02.150 --> 13:04.530
She's actually keeping up with Kataoka!

13:11.830 --> 13:13.290
That newbie's good!

13:13.370 --> 13:17.170
--Go! Go! Let's go! Let's go, Ogata!
--Is this really her second time riding?!

13:24.920 --> 13:27.130
You're not wimping out on me now, are you?

13:27.220 --> 13:31.560
The end result is clear,
as is the reason you showed up anyway.

13:31.640 --> 13:35.230
There are some people in this
world who can't say no to a challenge,

13:35.310 --> 13:38.650
even if they know they can't win.

13:38.730 --> 13:43.280
I'm one of them. And you are too, Rin Ogata.

13:43.360 --> 13:45.570
We're cut from the same cloth.

13:45.650 --> 13:49.110
The fact you accepted my challenge is proof of that.

13:49.200 --> 13:52.160
I think you might be wrong.

13:52.410 --> 13:55.290
I, umm, kind of just wanted to get a better look,

13:55.370 --> 13:59.960
to see what level the national champion is at...

14:00.040 --> 14:01.210
I'm sorry.

14:03.300 --> 14:06.380
<i>Plus, I wanted to feel that sensation again...</i>

14:06.470 --> 14:11.550
Hmph. I see. You're saying I'm the inferior one here.

14:11.640 --> 14:14.930
All right, then! I'll give you
another lap as a handicap!

14:15.020 --> 14:18.730
In exchange, we'll start
the race right now! You okay with that?!

14:18.810 --> 14:19.770
Yes!

14:19.850 --> 14:24.780
Wait, Tamayo! Rin doesn't know the course! Plus...!

14:27.320 --> 14:28.900
Kawai! What's going on here?!

14:28.990 --> 14:30.530
Oh, I forgot to tell you!

14:30.620 --> 14:32.950
They're in the middle of
moving construction materials,

14:33.030 --> 14:36.160
so it'll be about five minutes
until you can go through.

14:36.250 --> 14:39.080
For now, go around through Building #8.

14:39.170 --> 14:40.250
Urgh!

14:40.330 --> 14:44.550
Hishida! We're gonna start over
in front of the club building after all!

14:44.630 --> 14:45.590
Roger!

14:46.300 --> 14:50.760
Say, how hard is it to drive a RideBack anyway?

14:50.840 --> 14:53.600
It's simple, if you're just
going to ride it like normal.

14:53.680 --> 14:57.270
It comes with stuff like an
auto mode that keeps balance for you.

14:57.350 --> 15:01.270
But they're using manual mode;
even people with good coordination

15:01.350 --> 15:03.980
would have a hard time standing up at first.

15:04.070 --> 15:07.570
Then that really was a miraculous grand jete!

15:07.650 --> 15:08.820
Grand jete?

15:08.900 --> 15:12.570
It's a ballet term. It means "big jump."

15:12.660 --> 15:15.280
Is it really okay for us to go through here?

15:15.370 --> 15:18.580
It's fine. Anything goes.

15:18.660 --> 15:22.120
The thrill of RideBack racing
is in taking the "path without roads."

15:22.210 --> 15:24.670
Pres! What are you doing?!

15:24.750 --> 15:26.750
The student government's
gonna file another complaint!

15:26.840 --> 15:28.550
Bring it on, I say!

15:28.630 --> 15:29.840
Urgh...!

15:31.130 --> 15:32.800
See 'em?

15:32.890 --> 15:34.260
Nothing yet!

15:34.350 --> 15:36.470
Keep watching! Any minute now!

15:42.230 --> 15:43.190
There they are!

15:48.440 --> 15:49.820
Here we go!

15:50.320 --> 15:52.360
Ready...

15:52.700 --> 15:53.740
Start!

15:58.080 --> 16:00.750
You can do it, Rin!

16:01.500 --> 16:04.420
RideBacks are actually kind of cool!

16:04.500 --> 16:07.000
Oh! You've come to your senses!

16:07.090 --> 16:08.710
I have!

16:08.800 --> 16:10.590
That was Rin, wasn't it?

16:11.340 --> 16:12.720
Shoko!

16:13.640 --> 16:15.510
So, how is it going?

16:17.760 --> 16:20.220
Playtime is over now.

16:28.270 --> 16:31.150
<i>She's suddenly going faster...!</i>

16:33.030 --> 16:35.110
<i>That form... I saw it online!</i>

16:35.910 --> 16:37.280
<i>Let me think...</i>

16:43.750 --> 16:45.370
<i>What acceleration!</i>

16:45.460 --> 16:48.500
What?! Rin's using the Spread Legs Form too?!

16:48.590 --> 16:49.670
What's that?

16:49.750 --> 16:52.380
A high-speed mode where the RideBack's legs

16:52.470 --> 16:55.680
are spread forward and back,
and its center of gravity is lowered.

16:55.760 --> 17:00.350
It reduces air resistance,
but also makes high-speed turns harder.

17:00.430 --> 17:02.890
--Hishida! Are you watching their times?!
--What?

17:02.980 --> 17:05.770
I think the newbie is gaining on her!

17:09.320 --> 17:11.690
Kataoka! Are you letting her catch up?

17:11.780 --> 17:13.740
Shut up! You're interfering with the race!

17:14.610 --> 17:18.280
<i>A rookie who can barely ride</i>
<i>is catching up to me now...</i>

17:18.370 --> 17:19.490
<i>Is it natural talent?</i>

17:19.580 --> 17:21.620
<i>But can she handle this?</i>

17:48.770 --> 17:51.360
<i>My presumption was correct after all.</i>

17:51.440 --> 17:54.400
<i>She was willing to</i>
<i>accelerate so hard to catch up to me</i>

17:54.490 --> 17:57.030
<i>even if she risked plunging into the lake.</i>

17:57.110 --> 18:02.910
<i>She's hiding ferocious fangs</i>
<i>beneath that veil of hers...</i>

18:02.990 --> 18:06.960
Hishida. The Fuego fell
into the lake. Go pull her out.

18:22.890 --> 18:24.430
Come here, Fuego.

18:37.950 --> 18:42.410
--She's already past the water tower!
--So what?! What about Rin?!

18:44.330 --> 18:46.830
Okay, you're in charge!

18:46.910 --> 18:50.790
--Wait! I'm coming too!
--Oh! She's moving!

18:51.790 --> 18:54.250
Huh? She stopped again...

18:55.510 --> 18:57.090
That spot...

18:57.170 --> 18:58.220
Tamayo.

19:01.050 --> 19:04.550
I think Rin might be up ahead. Can you confirm?

19:11.440 --> 19:14.440
I like you. You still haven't given up.

19:14.900 --> 19:16.730
The race is back on!

19:16.820 --> 19:17.940
She's moving!

19:18.030 --> 19:19.990
--She's all right!
--Rin!

19:21.610 --> 19:23.570
She's closing in on her!

19:24.660 --> 19:27.040
I didn't know the Fuego could go so fast...

19:37.000 --> 19:39.380
Now let's see you bare your fangs!

19:41.970 --> 19:43.050
It's a dead heat!

19:45.050 --> 19:47.470
--You can do it!
--Come on, Rin!

19:48.430 --> 19:51.390
Y-You idiot! It'll happen
again if you turn at that speed!

20:11.660 --> 20:13.290
<i>What riding...!</i>

20:46.620 --> 20:50.910
The tests came back okay.
It's just a light concussion.

20:51.000 --> 20:55.330
I think the fact she didn't finish
the race might be her biggest concern.

20:55.420 --> 20:58.460
Hishida. There's still time to enter, right?

20:58.540 --> 21:00.300
Oh, you're awake?

21:00.380 --> 21:04.090
Huh? The titleholders have
already been sent their applications.

21:05.340 --> 21:07.300
Not me. Her.

21:08.470 --> 21:11.510
We'll finish this in another race, Rin Ogata.

21:11.600 --> 21:14.890
You start training hard tomorrow. Prepare yourself.

21:19.480 --> 21:20.440
Right!

21:27.820 --> 21:31.330
Suzuri said she's going to join the RideBack club too.

21:32.870 --> 21:36.920
She wanted to give it a try too
after she saw you out there.

21:39.790 --> 21:43.510
Is this what I should be doing?

21:43.590 --> 21:45.720
Why shouldn't it be?

21:45.800 --> 21:48.300
It really seemed to suit you!

21:56.730 --> 22:01.400
Even when he laughs

22:03.400 --> 22:08.990
I'm thinking of you before I realize it

22:12.030 --> 22:17.040
And the hands holding his

22:18.830 --> 22:24.300
feel your warmth, too

22:26.470 --> 22:30.220
Even if I cut out my recollections

22:30.300 --> 22:34.180
and drive them out of my heart

22:34.270 --> 22:37.930
or try to kick the memories out

22:38.020 --> 22:42.400
I still think of you

22:42.480 --> 22:46.900
Time now passes and seasons fly by

22:46.990 --> 22:50.740
Even if that smile starts to become hazy

22:50.820 --> 22:54.740
my heart will never forget you

22:54.830 --> 22:58.500
(even if we can never meet again)

22:58.580 --> 23:02.330
Even if I knock over photos of us smiling

23:02.420 --> 23:06.710
or try to hide my overflowing feelings

23:07.720 --> 23:10.970
my heart will never forget

23:11.680 --> 23:14.930
my memories with you

23:26.030 --> 23:41.020
New Hishida Theatre

23:27.110 --> 23:29.490
Rin's suddenly in the national tournament?!

23:29.570 --> 23:32.570
Really?! Seriously?!
Like, super-duper serious?!

23:32.660 --> 23:36.080
There are so few riders though,
that everyone who applies can compete.

23:35.870 --> 23:39.600
Next Episode:

23:35.870 --> 23:39.600
And There's the Flag

23:36.160 --> 23:38.830
Hooray for minor-league competitions!
Hooray for minor-league sports!

23:38.910 --> 23:40.250
Don't be happy that it's minor!
